[91.337988, "o", "h — 10 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ 4 steps folded · read ×3, grep · /app/cmd.sh, /app/jq_args.yaml, /app/active_users_report.json, +1 · nothing changed  /expand\r\nAll three deliverables are on disk and verified.\r\n\r\n**Files written**\r\n\r\n- `/app/active_users_report.json` — 346 active users, 2-space indent, keys in the required order.\r\n- `/app/cmd.sh` (mode 755, one line):\r\n  `jq --indent 2 '[.[] | select(.status == \"active\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split(\"T\")[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: .roles[0]}] | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json`\r\n- `/app/jq_args.yaml` — exactly two keys: `filter` (the filter string, unquoted by yq) and `args: [\"--indent 2\"]`, so the grader's `jq $(yq -r '.args[]' …) \"$(yq -r '.filter' …)\" /app/users.json > …` reconstructs the identical command.\r\n\r\n**Checks that passed** (run in the sub-turn, then spot-confirmed by r"]
[91.338025, "o", "eading the output)\r\n\r\n- `length` → 346; sort order confirmed with `sort -c`; every entry has a `YYYY-MM-DD` `last_login` and non-null `user_id` (0 violations).\r\n- `primary_role` is JSON `null` exactly where `roles` is empty (50 entries, e.g. user_id 6 `dudleynicholas`, 40 `david51`, 94 `jenny89`), and `role_count` matches the input role lengths.\r\n- Every reported username has `status: \"active\"` in `/app/users.json` (cross-checked by `user_id`; a first pass keyed on `username` showed 3 false positives because usernames repeat in the input).\r\n- Grader simulation `yq`-built command and `sh /app/cmd.sh` both diff clean against the delivered report (`YAML_REPRO_OK`, `CMD_OK`), so the YAML and the script cannot drift from the output.\r\n\r\nNothing left undone; `yq` is present, so the reconstruction was tested for real rather than assumed.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=11 surface=34a4546ddc81\r\n"]
